import ../../helpers/driver.dl

window quiet page:
    label "A page at rest"

window fitted page:
    label "A fitted page"
    style:
        the interface fits 640 by 480 pixels

set state to 0
set instance to an instance of quiet page with state (the address of state)
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 640 by 480 using fonts "regular" and "bold" with the test UI driver
require condition ((update UI view (the address of view)) = false) reporting "A static page scheduled another frame"
require condition (view's paint count = 1) reporting "The initial page was not painted"
require condition (view's layout's bounds' width = 576.0) reporting "Window margins were not applied to the initial layout"
set label to the UI layout for element (the control labeled "A page at rest" in (the address of instance)) in (view's layout)
require condition (label's bounds' width = 576.0) reporting "The initial label exceeds its available width"
set index to 0
loop while index < 100:
    require condition ((update UI view (the address of view)) = false) reporting "An idle page scheduled a frame"
    increment index
require condition (view's paint count = 1) reporting "An unchanged page was repainted"
request a UI redraw in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (view's paint count = 2) reporting "Explicit damage did not repaint the page"
set view's width to 800
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (view's paint count = 3) reporting "A resize did not repaint the page"
require condition (view's layout's bounds' width = 736.0) reporting "Ordinary window controls did not resize inside their margins"
require condition (label's bounds' width = 736.0) reporting "Automatic flow did not resize its children"
close the address of view
close the address of instance
set second to an instance of fitted page
set other to a UI view of (the address of second) sized 640 by 480 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view (the address of other)
require condition ((other's last cursor's x is finite) and (other's last cursor's y is finite)) reporting "Input used an uninitialized fitted viewport"
set paints to other's paint count
set other's width and other's height to 0
require condition ((update UI view (the address of other)) = false) reporting "A zero-sized surface kept scheduling frames"
require condition ((other's last cursor's x is finite) and (other's last cursor's y is finite)) reporting "A zero-sized surface produced invalid cursor coordinates"
set other's width to 640
set other's height to 480
ignore update UI view (the address of other)
require condition (other's paint count = (paints + 1)) reporting "Restoring the original size lost pending damage"
close the address of other
close the address of second
print line "Static pages sleep; damage and resizing repaint."
